I'll inspect how dockview mounts panel content in this project before changing anything.Let me read the actual current files to be sure of the exact code.I need to confirm dockview's DOM structure for overlay-rendered panels (that's what the snippet shows).## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
- You're right: `container-type` must live on **each panel's own wrapper**, not on the desktop root. Your DOM dump confirms it — dockview renders `renderer: 'always'` panels (which is exactly what `Desktop.vue → addAppPanel()` uses) into one absolutely positioned overlay per panel:
  ```html
  <div tabindex="-1" class="dv-render-overlay" style="left: 1679.99px; top: 34.9959px; width: 583px; height: 693.086px;"></div>
  ```
  That element is panel-sized, so making **it** a size container is what makes `@sm:` / `@lg:` inside a panel measure the panel. A rule living on the dockview root still only "names" the desktop; the containment has to be declared **on the panel wrapper element**, which is what this change does.

**Strategic Approach**
1. Target the panel wrapper **classes generated by dockview** (`.dv-render-overlay` for overlay/`always` panels — your panels — plus `.dv-content-container` for the DOM renderer used by restored/legacy layouts).
2. Put the rule where all other `.dv-*` overrides already live: `src/assets/main.css`, "Desktop" section. It must be global because the element is created by dockview JS — no Vue template can reach it.
3. Nothing else changes: no component, no store, no layout logic.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `container-type: inline-size` implies `contain: layout style inline-size` — **no paint containment**, so dropdowns/tooltips overflowing the panel are *not* clipped.
- Side effect to know about: inside the container, `position: fixed` descendants are positioned relative to the **panel**, not the viewport.
  - ✅ Global `<modal>` is safe — `src/components/Modal.vue` reparents itself to `this.$root.$el` on `mounted()`.
  - ✅ Reka/Radix portals (`Menubar*`, `Select`, `Popover`) teleport to `<body>` → unaffected.
  - ⚠️ `src/components/SelectionMenu.vue` is `fixed` + positioned with raw `clientX/clientY`; inside a chat panel it will now be offset. Same for inline daisyUI `.toast` blocks inside panels. Fix (if you want) is a one-line `<Teleport to="body">` in SelectionMenu — say the word.

**Target Files**
- `src/assets/main.css` (modify)

---

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

**`src/assets/main.css`** — one new documented block in the existing "Desktop" dockview section, declaring `container-type: inline-size` on the per-panel wrapper elements. No other line touched.

---

