## 4. Design-system notes & usage

**Usage inside any panel component**

```vue
<div class="p-4">
  <!-- 1 col in a narrow panel, 2 at 28rem (448px), 3 at 32rem (512px) -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 @md:grid-cols-2 @lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <div v-for="app in apps" :key="app.key" class="card bg-base-200 p-3">
      <span class="text-sm text-base-content/80">{{ app.name }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Behavior matrix**

| Panel width | `@sm:` (24rem) | `@md:` (28rem) | `@lg:` (32rem) | `@2xl:` (42rem) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 360px | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| 583px (your dump) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| full-screen / maximized | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |

**Anti-patterns**
- ❌ Re-declaring `@container` on a deep child (`<div class="@container">` inside a panel) — it becomes the *nearest* container, so `@lg:` then measures that inner box and your layout breaks when padding changes.
- ❌ Mixing viewport variants (`lg:grid-cols-3`) and container variants (`@lg:grid-cols-3`) for the same intent in a panel — pick container variants for anything that must survive a sash drag.
- ❌ Adding `overflow-hidden` around container-queried grids to "fix" overflow — it hides the real problem (the query is matching the wrong box).

**QA checklist**
- [ ] Drag a panel narrower than ~448px: `@md:` layouts collapse to one column, no horizontal overflow.
- [ ] After a project switch (layout restored from `localStorage`), restored panels still respond — the rule is on the panel wrapper class, not per panel instance.
- [ ] Text selection menu in a chat panel: expect it offset upward/leftward now (fixed → contained). Fix = `<Teleport to="body">` in `SelectionMenu.vue`; I can apply that next if you want.
- [ ] Panel dropdowns (`BranchSelector`, `ChatPanelHeader` ⋮ menu) still paint outside the panel bounds (no paint containment).
- [ ] Not needed for `VibeDesktop.vue` — it renders the active view directly in a `div`, no dockview, so viewport queries remain correct there.

**Scope note:** the rule applies to every dockview instance, so `FileExplorerPanel.vue`'s inner dockview also gains panel-relative queries for free. If you'd rather scope it to the desktop only, prefix the selectors with `.dv-dockview` — but the file-browser panels benefit from it as well, so I left it global.

